Refresh APC service list after save, same as DPD's (v0.137)

Dan asked how to grow the Available Services cache back up - turned out
opening the Service dropdown and arrow-keying through it does nothing at
all to the cache (that's just scrolling the one list already fetched
when the order loaded; no further API calls happen from that), so his
test couldn't have changed anything regardless of the v0.136 fix. The
real way to add more codes is for the live lookup itself to run again
against orders with different delivery weights/postcodes (explained to
Dan in chat, no code change needed for that part).

While checking this, found a real second bug alongside it: OrderEdit's
save mutation invalidates the "dpd-services" react-query cache key after
a successful save (so a changed delivery address/weight on that order
is reflected immediately), but never invalidated the matching
"apc-services" key - so APC's own list stayed stuck showing whatever was
eligible before the save, until the page was reloaded from scratch. Added
the missing invalidateQueries call right alongside DPD's.

